      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(web-search): align credential presence with usable providers",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWeb-search credential presence detection mixed ordinary provider options with real credentials. It could count non-credential fields as configured credentials while missing credential-equivalent plugin config such as SearXNG `baseUrl` and explicit keyless providers.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe detector now only counts direct or scoped `apiKey` values under `tools.web.search`, applies consistent SecretRef/env semantics, checks plugin `webSearch` credentials including `baseUrl`, and treats manifest-declared bundled providers with `requiresCredential: false` as configured when explicitly selected.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSecurity/audit and setup paths get fewer false positives from non-credential search options and fewer false negatives for explicitly selected keyless web-search providers. No live provider key is needed for the regression proof.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `OPENCLAW_VITEST_FS_MODULE_CACHE_PATH=/tmp/openclaw-vitest-cache-web-search-rebase node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/plugins/web-search-credential-presence.test.ts`\n- `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.core.test.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/core-test.tsbuildinfo`\n- `oxfmt --check` and `oxlint` on `src/plugins/web-search-credential-presence.ts` and `src/plugins/web-search-credential-presence.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check`\n\n## Proof\n\nThe local config matrix covers direct credentials, unresolved and resolved env SecretRefs, legacy env SecretRef strings, non-env SecretRefs, plugin `webSearch.apiKey`, plugin `webSearch.baseUrl`, explicit keyless providers, explicit credentialed providers without keys, unknown providers, and public artifact probe failures.\n",
        "branch": "llagy007/web-search-credential-presence-v2",
        "head_sha": "22aafd7ebc19022d00e3844853564d4bca547018",
        "author": "llagy007",
